# Dev / test / deploy (draft)

Full text: [docs/context/05-dev-test-deployment.md](docs/context/05-dev-test-deployment.md).

A feature is done when it has implementation + tests + observability + failure behavior + docs + repeatable validation. Compiling is not done.

Priority: correctness → observability → testability → maintainability → measured performance → sophistication.

- Contracts first: firmware ↔ packet ↔ decoder ↔ DB ↔ AI ↔ API ↔ dashboard. Golden packet fixtures. Synthetic node uses the same encoder as firmware.
- Test pyramid. Host unit tests without hardware. Simulation mandatory and seedable. HIL after unit tests.
- Separate versions: firmware, protocol, DB schema, config, features, model.
- Envs: development / simulation / hardware_test / staging / production. Modes: demo / field / calibration / experiment. Never present simulated data as real.
- Production disables unrestricted fault injection. No secrets in git.
- Consistent names: `node_id`, `event_confidence`, `sensor_quality`, `received_at`, `measurement_time`. Explicit units.
- Do not start with the AI model. Smallest real data path first (after conflict sign-off).
- Do not reuse ADR numbers 001–008.

Existing execution path (D1 accepted, D2/MVN) remains implemented law until the matrix is decided.
